cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use slopbench or its panel data, please cite it as below."
title: "slopbench: measuring package hallucination and its recurrence in AI model output"
type: software
authors:
  - name: Blvkware
    website: "https://blvkware.dev"
repository-code: "https://github.com/rxslice/slopbench"
url: "https://blvkware.dev/ai-package-hallucination-data/"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.1
date-released: 2026-11-14
abstract: >-
  slopbench measures how often a language model or coding agent names a
  software dependency that does not exist, or exists without adoption, on
  PyPI, npm or crates.io, and how often it names the same invented package
  in independent samples of the same prompt. Only recurring names can be
  pre-registered by an attacker (slopsquatting), so recurrence is the headline.
keywords:
  - slopsquatting
  - package hallucination
  - LLM security
  - software supply chain
  - AI coding agents
  - benchmark
